{
  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7514": {
      "title": "Instructor &amp; Director of Clinical Education",
      "description": "Oregon Institute of Technology Portal | Instructor &amp; Director of Clinical Education Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs Campus Locations Human Resources Oregon Tech Instructor & Director of Clinical Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The initial review of applications will begin October 16, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted after the initial review date until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. Therefore, at the discretion of the University, materials received after the initial review date may not receive full consideration. To apply, upload the following elements to your application: Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Resume Transcripts (Unofficial) Letter of Recommendation Professional References List License/Certification Other Document For additional information, please contact the Office of Human Resources: oithr@oit.edu Posting Details Position Details Position Type Non Tenure Working Title Instructor & Director of Clinical Education Classification Title Instructor College/Division College of Health, Arts & Sciences (HAS) Department Integrated Clinical Sciences Hiring Unit Work Location Klamath Falls Appointment FTE (%) 1.0 Position Terms/Mo 9 Full/Part time Full Time Annual Salary 62,000 Position Summary Department Summary The Integrated Clinical Sciences ( ICS ) Department brings together programs in Medical Laboratory Science, Respiratory Care, Sleep Health/Polysomnography, and Emergency Medical Services to support a cohesive, student-centered approach to healthcare education. These programs share a foundation in applied clinical science, evidence-based practice, and patient-centered care, preparing graduates to contribute across diagnostic, therapeutic, and pre-hospital environments. Consistent with institutional priorities for student learning and workforce responsiveness, ICS programs emphasize competency-based education, clinical experiences, and preparation for national certification and licensure. Students develop the knowledge, technical skills, and professional behaviors necessary to meet current and emerging healthcare needs in diverse practice settings. The department reflects the collaborative nature of modern healthcare by aligning disciplines across the continuum of patient care—from emergency response to diagnosis, treatment, and ongoing management. Programs are delivered across multiple modalities, including campus-based and online formats, expanding access for both traditional students and working professionals. In particular, Sleep Health and Polysomnographic Technology programs are offered fully online, supporting flexible pathways for students in clinical practice. Through this integrated structure, the ICS Department supports clear academic pathways, fosters interdisciplinary awareness, and aligns program outcomes with institutional goals for academic quality, student success, and community impact. For additional information regarding the ICS Department, please visit: https://catalog.oit.edu/departments/ ICS /overview Position Summary The Department of Respiratory Care within the College of Health, Arts, & Sciences on Oregon Tech’s Klamath Falls, OR campus invites applications for the Non Tenure Track role of Instructor & Director of Clinical Education. The position provides instruction in both respiratory care didactic and laboratory courses. Instruction may occur in on-campus, laboratory, clinical, simulation, and online learning environments. This position also serves as the Director of Clinical Education ( DCE ) for the respiratory care program. The Director of Clinical Education role includes oversight and coordination of student clinical experiences across multiple healthcare facilities and clinical settings. Responsibilities include clinical scheduling and placement, maintaining relationships with clinical affiliates and preceptors, assisting with affiliation agreements and onboarding processes, monitoring student clinical performance and progression, ensuring compliance with program and clinical site requirements, and supporting accreditation standards related to clinical education. The position also involves ongoing communication and collaboration with healthcare partners to help ensure students receive high-quality clinical learning experiences aligned with current respiratory care practice standards. The successful incumbent must be well-rounded and creative in their teaching methods and approaches. They should have the ability to present materials to students while demonstrating the use of relevant medical equipment and current respiratory care practices. Although teaching is an essential part of this position, the ability to work with students as an academic advisor and engage in applied research and/or scholarly activity is also important. Further, the position will work closely with the Program Director in the ongoing development and revision of evidence-based curriculum for both on-campus and online learning environments. This includes supporting curriculum alignment with current NBRC credentialing expectations, CoARC accreditation standards, AARC guidelines, evolving healthcare practices, and workforce needs. Minimum Requirements Additional Requirements Bachelor’s degree in Respiratory Care or in a related field. Applicants hired without a master’s degree will be expected to complete a master’s degree within a timeframe established at hire. Registered Respiratory Therapist ( RRT ) granted by the National Board or Respiratory Care ( NBRC ) Respiratory Care Licensure by the State of Oregon At least 5 years of hospital care experience with educational background in academia, medical facility or student/new hire orientation Preferred Qualifications Master’s or terminal degree Previous or current instructor in a respiratory care program Experience with CoARC accreditation Familiarity with conducting institutional assessments Experience in student advisement Current AARC membership Application Information Recruitment Type External Application Screening Begins 10/16/2026 Job Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicant The initial review of applications will begin October 16, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted after the initial review date until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. Therefore, at the discretion of the University, materials received after the initial review date may not receive full consideration. To apply, upload the following elements to your application: Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Resume Transcripts (Unofficial) Letter of Recommendation Professional References List License/Certification Other Document For additional information, please contact the Office of Human Resources: oithr@oit.edu Background/Pre-Employment Check Any offer of employment to a successful candidate will be conditioned upon the University’s receipt of a satisfactory background check, motor vehicle check, physical abilities check, and/or any other conditions of employment contained in the vacancy announcement. AA/EEO Statement Oregon Tech is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Educator and Employer. The University does not discriminate in access to its educational programs and activities, or with respect to hiring, or the terms and conditions of employment, on the basis of age, color, disability, marital status, national origin, race, religion or creed, sex or gender, gender identity or gender expression, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other basis in law. Oregon Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in its services, programs, activities, education and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, contact the Office of Human Resource at 541-885-1028 or oithr@oit.edu . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Resume Transcripts (Unofficial) Letter of Recommendation Professional References List License/Certification Other Document Contact Us: Office of Human Resources 3201 Campus Dr. Klamath Falls, Oregon 97601 Phone: (541) 885-1120 Email: oithr@oit.edu Website: http://www.oit.edu/hr Policies | Campus Safety | Campus Alerts | Directory | Site Index Connect with us: | | To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7513": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor (Academic)",
      "description": "Oregon Institute of Technology Portal | Assistant/Associate Professor (Academic) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs Campus Locations Human Resources Oregon Tech Assistant/Associate Professor (Academic) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The initial review of applications will begin October 15, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted after the initial review date until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. Therefore, at the discretion of the University, materials received after the initial review date may not receive full consideration. To apply, upload the following elements to your application: Required Documents Cover Letter Transcripts (Unofficial) Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy License/Certification Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents Resume Letter of Recommendation Professional References List Other Document For additional information, please contact the Office of Human Resources: oithr@oit.edu Posting Details Position Details Position Type Tenure Track Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor (Academic) Classification Title Assistant or Associate Professor College/Division College of Health, Arts & Sciences (HAS) Department Physical Therapy Hiring Unit Work Location Klamath Falls Appointment FTE (%) 1.00 Position Terms/Mo 12 Full/Part time Full Time Annual Salary Up to 105,000; commensurate with education and experience Position Summary Department Summary About the Doctor of Physical Therapy Program: The Doctor of Physical Therapy ( DPT ) is a joint Oregon Tech and Oregon Health & Science University ( OHSU ) program that will provide a comprehensive entry-level and post-baccalaureate DPT education, with the unique focus of preparing high-quality graduates with the skills to become practitioners of choice and leaders in rural physical therapy practice. The DPT program will ensure graduates develop competence in the diagnosis and treatment of patients with health or medical conditions that may affect movement and mobility. Graduates will complete all eligibility requirements to sit for the state licensure exam and will be prepared for employment as autonomous practitioners in a variety of clinical settings. As led by the American Physical Therapy Association ( APTA ), graduates will be encouraged to pursue advanced learning and mentorship opportunities, including but not limited to: Residency and Fellowship ABPTS Specialist Certification Credentialed Clinical Instructor Program Post-Professional Degree Leadership Development Advanced Proficiency Pathways Clinical Training Sites Clinical training sites throughout Southern Oregon and in other rural communities have been identified, serving the essential critical function for preparing practitioners for the exciting generalist roles required in serving rural health communities. In addition, we seek to provide an important linkage between students on rotations, clinical and core faculty given the joint program with Oregon Tech and OHSU . Oregon’s academic medical center, OHSU , provides experiences across a range of clinical settings including high complexity acute care and ICU , pediatrics, and outpatient rehab across a range of specialty areas. https://www.oit.edu/academics/degrees/doctor-of-physical-therapy Position Summary This position is a 12-month core faculty position on the Klamath Falls campus in the College of Health, Arts, and Sciences, Department of Physical Therapy. The OIT / OHSU DPT Program’s unique themes include Rural Healthcare, Evidence-Informed Practice, and Emotional Intelligence. The successful candidate will be part of a core team educating, mentoring, and advising students to cultivate the knowledge, psychomotor skills, and professional behavior required for entry-level clinicians. Core faculty will maintain a mix of teaching, scholarship, service, and clinical activity to maintain licensure, currency in the field, and meet accreditation requirements. Minimum Requirements Additional Requirements Licensed or eligible for physical therapist licensure in Oregon within 3 months of start Academic Doctoral degree (PhD, EdD, DSc, etc.) with contemporary expertise in the assigned teaching areas Teaching Expertise and research agenda to meet 2024 CAPTE Standards in an accredited DPT program Preferred Qualifications 3 or more years academic teaching experience Experience in assisting with CAPTE accreditation Evidence of clinical practice in rural areas Previous involvement of students in research activities Prior successful grant funding Application Information Recruitment Type External Application Screening Begins 10/15/2026 Job Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicant The initial review of applications will begin October 15, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted after the initial review date until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. Therefore, at the discretion of the University, materials received after the initial review date may not receive full consideration. To apply, upload the following elements to your application: Required Documents Cover Letter Transcripts (Unofficial) Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy License/Certification Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents Resume Letter of Recommendation Professional References List Other Document For additional information, please contact the Office of Human Resources: oithr@oit.edu Background/Pre-Employment Check Any offer of employment to a successful candidate will be conditioned upon the University’s receipt of a satisfactory background check, motor vehicle check, physical abilities check, and/or any other conditions of employment contained in the vacancy announcement. AA/EEO Statement Oregon Tech is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Educator and Employer. The University does not discriminate in access to its educational programs and activities, or with respect to hiring, or the terms and conditions of employment, on the basis of age, color, disability, marital status, national origin, race, religion or creed, sex or gender, gender identity or gender expression, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other basis in law. Oregon Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in its services, programs, activities, education and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, contact the Office of Human Resource at 541-885-1028 or oithr@oit.edu . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Transcripts (Unofficial) Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy License/Certification Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents Resume Letter of Recommendation Professional References List Other Document Contact Us: Office of Human Resources 3201 Campus Dr. Klamath Falls, Oregon 97601 Phone: (541) 885-1120 Email: oithr@oit.edu Website: http://www.oit.edu/hr Policies | Campus Safety | Campus Alerts | Directory | Site Index Connect with us: | | To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
