    "https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7599": {
      "title": "Visiting Instructor, Respiratory Care",
      "description": "Oregon Institute of Technology Portal | Visiting Instructor, Respiratory Care Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs Campus Locations Human Resources Oregon Tech Visiting Instructor, Respiratory Care Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The review of applications will begin November 30, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted after the initial review date until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. Therefore, at the discretion of the University, materials received after the initial review date may not receive full consideration. To apply, upload the following elements to your application: Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Professional References List Optional Documents Resume Transcripts (Unofficial) Teaching Philosophy License/Certification Other Document For additional information, please contact the Office of Human Resources: oithr@oit.edu Posting Details Position Details Position Type Non Tenure Working Title Visiting Instructor, Respiratory Care Classification Title Visiting Instructor College/Division College of Health, Arts & Sciences (HAS) Department Integrated Clinical Sciences Hiring Unit Work Location Klamath Falls Appointment FTE (%) 1.0 Position Terms/Mo 9 months Full/Part time Full Time Annual Salary $56,000 - $62,000 Position Summary Department Summary ICS Department Overview The Integrated Clinical Sciences ( ICS ) Department brings together programs in Medical Laboratory Science, Respiratory Care, Sleep Health/Polysomnography, and Emergency Medical Services to support a cohesive, student-centered approach to healthcare education. These programs share a foundation in applied clinical science, evidence-based practice, and patient-centered care, preparing graduates to contribute across diagnostic, therapeutic, and pre-hospital environments. Consistent with institutional priorities for student learning and workforce responsiveness, ICS programs emphasize competency-based education, clinical experiences, and preparation for national certification and licensure. Students develop the knowledge, technical skills, and professional behaviors necessary to meet current and emerging healthcare needs in diverse practice settings. The department reflects the collaborative nature of modern healthcare by aligning disciplines across the continuum of patient care—from emergency response to diagnosis, treatment, and ongoing management. Programs are delivered across multiple modalities, including campus-based and online formats, expanding access for both traditional students and working professionals. In particular, Sleep Health and Polysomnographic Technology programs are offered fully online, supporting flexible pathways for students in clinical practice. Through this integrated structure, the ICS Department supports clear academic pathways, fosters interdisciplinary awareness, and aligns program outcomes with institutional goals for academic quality, student success, and community impact. For additional departmental information, please visit: https://catalog.oit.edu/departments/ ICS /overview Position Summary The Visiting Instructor of Respiratory Care provides high-quality instruction and mentorship to students enrolled in both the on-campus and Degree Advancement Respiratory Care programs. This position supports student learning through lecture, laboratory, and clinical instruction while promoting the mission and values of Oregon Institute of Technology. The Visiting Instructor collaborates with program faculty to ensure curriculum consistency, fosters professional development, and contributes to student success through active engagement and assessment. Minimum Requirements Additional Requirements Bachelor’s degree in Respiratory Care or a related health science field. Registered Respiratory Therapist ( RRT ) credential. Current licensure or eligibility for licensure in the state of Oregon. Minimum of two (2) years of clinical respiratory care experience. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in Respiratory Care, Education, or a related field. Prior teaching experience in an academic or clinical setting. Experience with simulation-based instruction and/or online teaching platforms. Active involvement in professional organizations such as AARC or NBRC . Five (5) years of clinical respiratory care experience. Application Information Recruitment Type External Application Screening Begins 11/30/2026 Job Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicant The review of applications will begin November 30, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted after the initial review date until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. Therefore, at the discretion of the University, materials received after the initial review date may not receive full consideration. To apply, upload the following elements to your application: Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Professional References List Optional Documents Resume Transcripts (Unofficial) Teaching Philosophy License/Certification Other Document For additional information, please contact the Office of Human Resources: oithr@oit.edu Background/Pre-Employment Check Any offer of employment to a successful candidate will be conditioned upon the University’s receipt of a satisfactory background check, motor vehicle check, physical abilities check, and/or any other conditions of employment contained in the vacancy announcement. AA/EEO Statement Oregon Tech is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Educator and Employer. The University does not discriminate in access to its educational programs and activities, or with respect to hiring, or the terms and conditions of employment, on the basis of age, color, disability, marital status, national origin, race, religion or creed, sex or gender, gender identity or gender expression, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other basis in law. Oregon Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in its services, programs, activities, education and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, contact the Office of Human Resource at 541-885-1028 or oithr@oit.edu . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Professional References List Optional Documents Resume Transcripts (Unofficial) Teaching Philosophy License/Certification Other Document Contact Us: Office of Human Resources 3201 Campus Dr. Klamath Falls, Oregon 97601 Phone: (541) 885-1120 Email: oithr@oit.edu Website: http://www.oit.edu/hr Policies | Campus Safety | Campus Alerts | Directory | Site Index Connect with us: | | To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
